6. ENFORCEMENT

Any use of the Software outside this Agreement is unlicensed. It is a breach
of contract and an infringement of copyright, and the Owner will pursue it
to the full extent of civil and criminal law, in Thailand and in the country
where it happens.

Thailand - Copyright Act B.E. 2537 (1994), as amended:

  - Sections 30 and 69. Reproducing, adapting, communicating to the public
    or renting out a computer program without permission: a fine of THB
    20,000 to 200,000. For commercial purposes: imprisonment of 6 months to
    4 years, or a fine of THB 100,000 to 800,000, or both.

  - Sections 31 and 70. Dealing in infringing copies for profit (selling,
    offering, distributing, importing): a fine of THB 10,000 to 100,000.
    For commercial purposes: imprisonment of 3 months to 2 years, or a fine
    of THB 50,000 to 400,000, or both.

  - Sections 53/1 to 53/6 and 70/1. Removing rights management information,
    circumventing technological protection measures, or supplying a tool or
    service that does, is a separate criminal offence.

  - Section 73. A repeat offence within five years of the last penalty:
    twice the penalty.

  - Section 74. The directors and managers of a company are jointly liable
    with it.

  - Section 64. Damages, including lost profit and the cost of enforcement;
    up to double where the infringement was intentional and made the work
    widely available to the public.

  - Sections 75 and 76. Infringing copies and the things used to make them
    are forfeited or destroyed at the infringer's expense, and half of the
    fine is paid to the Owner.

United States - for infringement there:

  - 17 U.S.C. 504. Statutory damages of up to USD 150,000 per work for
    wilful infringement.

  - 17 U.S.C. 506 and 18 U.S.C. 2319. Criminal infringement: fines and
    imprisonment.

  - 17 U.S.C. 1201 to 1204 (DMCA). Circumventing technical protection or
    removing copyright management information: up to USD 500,000 and 5
    years' imprisonment for a first wilful offence committed for gain.

Every other country: the Berne Convention, the WIPO Copyright Treaty and the
TRIPS Agreement protect the Software without registration, and that
country's copyright and anti-circumvention laws apply.

In addition You agree that:

  - the Owner may obtain an immediate court order to stop the breach,
    without having to prove actual loss;

  - You must hand over to the Owner all money and other benefit received
    from the breach, on top of damages;

  - You must pay the Owner's reasonable legal, investigation and
    enforcement costs;

  - the Owner may report infringing copies to hosts, stores, marketplaces
    and payment providers and have them removed.

The penalties above are those in force when this text was written; the law
in force at the time of the breach applies. A delay in enforcing is not a
waiver.


